<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">cooking</ansi> (skill)

Cooking is the art of preparing food and meals. A well-prepared meal can
restore health, boost stamina, or steady the mind. Adventurers depend on good
food to sustain them through hardship. The skill is governed by
<ansi fg="yellow">Perception</ansi>, since proper taste and balance matter more than brute force.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">hearth</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             The Kitchen is located in Startland.
  Materials: Fresh ingredients from foraging, hunting, and vendors.
             Find them on the ground in the Kitchen or loot from mobs.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

The recipe list for cooking is being documented as new recipes are added.
Check back soon for updates on available meals.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Using Meals ━━━</ansi>

Crafted meals are used with the <ansi fg="command">eat</ansi> command:

  <ansi fg="command">eat meal</ansi>

They apply their effect immediately. Check <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi> to see what you
are carrying, and <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> to see active effects.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Cooking improves through use. Each completed cook attempt (success or failure)
has a chance to advance the skill. Cooking progresses faster per use than
combat skills because crafting opportunities are less frequent.

There is no trainer for cooking — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including cooking ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin cooking a recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">eat <item></ansi>         Consume a cooked meal.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current cooking skill level.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help craft</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help eat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>
